-- The designer drugs, armor accessories and new body armor from Rifts World
-- Book Ten: Juicer Uprising, printed 61-71. Eighteen rows.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-juicer-uprising-gear-a.sql
--
-- The book has a TEXT LAYER, so this was read with scripts/read-columns.py and
-- transcribed rather than OCR'd. The printed-to-PDF offset is ZERO.
--
-- FIRST OF THREE GEAR BATCHES, and the gap here is close to total: of the ~35
-- items this book prices, exactly ONE was already in the catalog
-- (c-18-laser-pistol). Everything below is new.
--
-- CONVENTIONS, taken from the catalog rather than the book:
--   - A PRICE RANGE stores its LOW end in `cost` and the printed range in
--     `cost_note`. That is the CA-1/CA-2 Dead Boy precedent, and it is why the
--     drugs read 30, 150, 250, 300 and 65 rather than an invented midpoint.
--   - Dice-valued and conditional damage lives in `damage` as printed text.
--     Every armor here that hits back does so on a body slam, which is a rule
--     rather than a weapon, so it is written out rather than reduced.
--   - `mdc` is an integer, so Super-Hide Armor - whose M.D.C. genuinely VARIES
--     with what it was made from - stores 70, the bottom of the ordinary range,
--     and the description carries the whole of it.
--
-- TWO PLACES THE BOOK DISAGREES WITH ITSELF, both recorded rather than
-- silently resolved. Titan Plate Armor is 195 M.D.C. on its own page and 180 in
-- the Titan Juicer O.C.C.'s equipment list; the item page wins, because it is
-- the entry that exists to state the item's numbers. Dragon Skin Combat Armor
-- is listed at 100 M.D.C. in the Dragon Juicer's equipment, which falls inside
-- the 70-100 range Super-Hide Armor's own page prints, so there is nothing to
-- resolve there - just worth saying so before somebody else finds it.
--
-- ONE TEXT-LAYER REPAIR: the Super-Hide price prints as "106x10,000 credits" in
-- the extracted text. That is 1D6x10,000 - the D read as a 0 - and it is the
-- same class of damage as the 4D6xlO and !D4xlOO all over this book, where l is
-- a 1 and O is a 0. Fixed by knowing what the value has to look like, which is
-- the only thing that fixes any of them.
--
-- Pure ASCII with LF line endings, comments included, per PR #93 and #101.
-- ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING, not DO UPDATE: every row here is new, and
-- nothing in this file should ever overwrite a curated value.

INSERT INTO gear (slug, name, system, category, weight_lbs, cost, cost_note, damage, is_mega_damage,
                  range, payload, rate_of_fire, mdc, description, source_book) VALUES
('drug-boing-go', 'Boing-go', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 30, 'Black market 30-60 credits per dose', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Designer drug. A powerful stimulant, roughly equal to drinking five pots of coffee and taking a hit of speed. Duration: 24+2D6 hours per dose. Bonuses: +1 on initiative; the user feels no fatigue and CANNOT sleep for the duration, so productivity over a full day can be three to four times normal. Penalties: hyper, fidgety and easily bored, and unable to sleep even when he wants to. Coming down leaves him exhausted and needing ten hours of sleep; forced to function without it, all combat bonuses, melee attacks, speed and skill proficiencies are HALVED. Addictiveness: HIGH - once a week for a month, or three times in one week, and the character is hooked: cannot sleep, hyper-active, -5% on skills, and losing 5 lbs (2.3 kg) a week despite a voracious appetite. After four months the addict collapses from exhaustion and needs detox. Juicer Uprising p.61-63.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('drug-crash', 'Crash', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 150, 'Black market 150-300 credits per dose', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Designer drug. A combination that gives its user a feeling of power, strength and invincibility. Duration: 1D4 hours. Bonuses: +1D4x10+10 S.D.C., +10 to P.E. and all bonuses that follow from it, +6 to P.S., +6 to Speed, +1 attack per melee, +8 to save versus horror factor, and the character is bold, fearless and aggressive. Penalties: bold enough to be talked into pointless brawls and stupid risks, and likely to ignore pain, injury and blood loss. THE CRASH IS THE POINT: nausea and vomiting 1D4 times an hour for 2D4 hours, pounding head, ringing ears, blurred vision, cannot walk straight or concentrate - -70% on skills, -6 on initiative, and speed, melee actions and combat bonuses halved, for 24 hours, doubled if he was also drinking. Addictiveness: MINIMUM, because the crash is so terrible most people never touch it twice. Twice a week makes an addict, and an addict crashes into something close to a coma: -90% on skills, -10 initiative, speed down 90%, one melee action, no combat bonuses, for 96 hours or until the next hit. After six months, roll daily for cardiac arrest (01-50%) or collapse (51-00%). A crash addict who survives the Juicer conversion has his life expectancy HALVED, to three years or less. Juicer Uprising p.63.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('drug-juice', 'Juice', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 250, 'Black market 250-500 credits per dose', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Designer drug, and the preferred Wannabe drug - a stimulant cocktail advertised to make users "tough as juicers." Duration: 1D6 hours. Bonuses: +4D6 S.D.C., +4 to P.S. and P.E., +3 to P.P., +1 attack per melee, +3D6 to Speed, +8 to save versus horror factor. The character feels no pain, is unaffected by shock, and CAN FIGHT UNTIL REDUCED TO -5 HIT POINTS. Penalties: filled with unreasoning rage and likely to answer any provocation violently - and since he cannot feel pain, likely to be crippled fighting or running on broken bones. When it wears off: -5 on initiative and all skills, combat bonuses and attacks halved, and 4D6 minutes later he collapses into a coma-like sleep for 2D4 hours that only strong psychic measures will break. A second dose the same day works for 3D6 minutes and then costs 4D6 hours of unconsciousness. Addictiveness: MEDIUM - four times a week makes an addict, who needs a dose daily and is tense and short-tempered without one: -10% on skills, -2 initiative, combat bonuses reduced by two, one attack lost. Juicer Uprising p.63.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('drug-mega', 'Mega', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 300, 'Black market 300-600 credits per dose', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Designer drug: a synthetic steroid that increases strength and toughness, and must be taken for weeks before it works. Duration: SPECIAL - one pill a day for 1D4+3 days straight before the effects appear, and one a week thereafter to keep them. Bonuses: +1D4x10 lbs of weight and muscle mass, +4D6+20 S.D.C., +4 to P.S., +2 to P.E.; minimum P.S. becomes 17. Can lift twice what an equivalent person could, lasts four times longer before exhaustion, stays alert and fully efficient for up to three days (72 hours) without sleep, and typically needs only five hours a night. The results are staggering enough that a Wannabe on Mega looks like he has had the treatment. Penalties: every two weeks after the treatment, save versus lethal poison or roll - 01-40% sleepless for 1D6 days at -1 to combat and -5% to skills; 41-70% over-stressed, and any feat of strength or combat action that month costs 1D6 plus P.S. bonus DIRECTLY TO HIT POINTS; 71-90% the same 1D6 times that month; 91-00% HEART ATTACK, hit points to zero, save versus coma and death, and 1D4+1 weeks in hospital. Addictiveness: LOW - a month without it clears the body entirely. Juicer Uprising p.63-65.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('drug-rush', 'Rush', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 65, 'Black market 65-120 credits per dose', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Designer drug that heightens the senses, speed and reflexes. Duration: 1D6x10 minutes. Bonuses: +1 attack per melee, +3 on initiative, +1 to strike, +2 to parry and dodge, +3 to roll with impact, +10 to Speed, +5% on general skill performance and +10% on skills needing dexterity and control - surgery, forgery, lock picking, piloting, acrobatics, gymnastics, climbing, juggling. The character becomes keenly aware of smell, taste, hearing and touch. Penalties: good and bad smells are twice as potent, competing sounds jangle the nerves and break concentration (-10% on skills), and the user is irritable and cranky. Addictiveness: MEDIUM - four times a week makes an addict, craving it 1D4 times daily. He keeps every bonus while high, but is so emotionally dependent that without it he believes himself clumsy and incompetent: -1 attack, -3 initiative, -2 strike, -3 parry and dodge, -3 roll with impact, -10% on skills, Speed down 20%, and food, sound and touch all seem dulled. Juicer Uprising p.64-65.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('sensor-jammers', 'Sensor Jammers', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 20000, 'Black market 20,000 credits to install into a suit of armor', NULL, 0, NULL, 'E-Clip; eight continuous hours, and each activation spends ten minutes of charge whether used that long or not', NULL, NULL, 'Armor accessory. Fiber-optic arrays and insulating materials that jam thermal and radar signatures and diffuse laser targeting. Active, the wearer has only a 15% chance of being detected by standard thermal and radar detectors and optics, guided missiles are -2 to strike (a volley of four or more is also -2, rolled once for the volley), and laser aiming systems lose their targeting bonus. Destroyed once more than half the armor M.D.C. is gone. Fits LIGHT OR MEDIUM armor of 50 M.D.C. or less only - tried on power armor and vehicles and found useless against their size, energy supply and heat signature - and useless on anything over 10 feet (3 m) tall. Juicers who specialise in infiltration love it. Juicer Uprising p.66.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('combat-gauntlets', 'Combat Gauntlets', 'rifts', 'weapon', 4.0, 5000, 'Black market 5,000 credits per gauntlet', 'Crush/squeeze 1D6 M.D. A normal human punching with them does 2D6 S.D.C. plus P.S. bonus; a Juicer, Crazy, borg or other augmented human does 1 M.D. on a normal punch or 1D6 M.D. on a power punch, which counts as two attacks. Supernatural P.S. adds +4 M.D. to hand to hand damage.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Gauntlets using the same mechanical muscles as borgs and power armor, giving the wearer a robotic strength of 26. Lets an augmented human inflict mega-damage with his punches while his hands stay protected. Useful as tools as well as weapons - the wearer can grip with mechanical strength. Juicer Uprising p.66.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('combat-vambraces', 'Combat Vambraces', 'rifts', 'weapon', 15.0, 40000, 'Black market 40,000 credits', 'Restrained punch 6D6 S.D.C. plus P.S. bonus; full strength punch 1D4 M.D.; power punch 2D4 M.D., counting as two melee attacks.', 1, NULL, 'Rechargeable battery with an energy life of eight hours', NULL, NULL, 'A piece of POWER ARMOR that covers an entire arm, strapped on or built into a suit of environmental armor, with a robotic P.S. of 24. Only a Juicer or a Crazy can use it - a normal human risks broken bones. It can be fitted with bionic or power armor weapon systems, purchased separately. Only ONE vambrace can be built into a suit of non-powered armor. The weight adds to the armor. Juicer Uprising p.67.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('grenade-bracers', 'Grenade Bracers', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 800, 'Black market 800 credits per bracer; grenades not included', NULL, 0, NULL, 'Three grenades per bracer, six if one is worn on each arm', NULL, NULL, 'Armor accessory: a bracer holding three grenades on the forearm on magnetic clip holders. To take one, the wearer grips it and twists clockwise, which releases the clip automatically. Fits normal body armor, Combat Vambraces, bionic limbs or power armor. Juicer Uprising p.67.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('forearm-grenade-launchers', 'Forearm Grenade-Launchers', 'rifts', 'weapon', 3.0, 2000, 'Black market 2,000 credits per forearm; 8,000 if a voice-activated launch system is built into the armor', 'Varies with grenade type.', 1, '600 feet (183 m)', 'Three grenades per forearm', 'One at a time, or in volleys of two or three', NULL, 'Grenade Bracers with electromagnetic launch systems added to the magnetic clips and a laser targeting system. The wearer aims the laser and presses a firing stud; it can be built into a glove or the wrist, or computerised as a VOICE COMMAND launcher. The weight adds to the armor. Juicer Uprising p.67.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('forearm-vibro-blades', 'Forearm Vibro-Blades (UTI)', 'rifts', 'weapon', NULL, 4000, 'Black market 4,000 credits for the double blade, 8,000 for the tri-blade', 'Double blade 2D6 M.D.; tri-blade 3D6 M.D.', 1, 'Hand to hand', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Mounted on the forearms of body armor and extending two or three vibro-blades at need. Juicers and Crazies are particularly fond of them, since they force the fight to hand to hand range where an augmented human has an enormous edge over a normal one. Juicer Uprising p.67.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('rocket-boots', 'Rocket Boots', 'rifts', 'gear', NULL, 30000, 'Black market 30,000 credits; 2,000 more to build into a suit of mega-damage environmental armor', NULL, 0, NULL, 'E-Clip; twenty jumps per standard clip', NULL, NULL, 'Footgear with focused explosive charges in the soles, powerful enough to throw the wearer up to 60 feet (18.3 m) into the air, and the rage among Juicers and Crazies. An Acrobatics or Gymnastics roll, treated as a back flip, lets the wearer turn in mid-air, dodge at +1, land behind someone, move 10-20 feet (3-6 m) laterally, or land on a rooftop or branch - all in two seconds. Each rocket jump counts as one melee action. NON-AUGMENTED humans and D-Bees risk injury every time: roll 16 or higher or the manoeuvre fails and the landing is bad, for 2D6 S.D.C. and the loss of initiative, and body armor does not protect against it. Broken legs, sprained ankles and pulled ligaments are common, and Juicer Wannabes keep trying anyway. Cybernetic or bionic legs remove the penalty entirely. Juicer Uprising p.67-68.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('titan-plate-armor', 'Titan Plate Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 250.0, 85000, 'Black market 85,000 credits for the standard non-environmental version, 110,000 for the full environmental suit, which adds 30 lbs (13.6 kg). Northern Gun is developing a knock-off reportedly 10% cheaper.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 195, 'Built by Ultra-Tech Incorporated for the Titan Juicer, and usable by giant-sized D-Bees of 8-12 feet (2.4 to 3.65 m). Thick heavy plates in the alloys used for power armor and cyborg armor: massive protection at some cost in mobility, leaving a Titan almost as well armored as a soldier in power armor. MINIMUM HEIGHT 7 feet (2.1 m) and minimum P.S. 24 - it does not accommodate smaller wearers. Variable mobility: at a normal P.S. of 40+ or a supernatural P.S. of 25+, -15% prowl, -5% climb, swim, acrobatics and gymnastics, speed reduced 10%. Weaker wearers, down to P.S. 25 normal or 20 supernatural, are -30% prowl, -15% to the rest, speed reduced 40%. Below that the wearer CANNOT MOVE AT ALL. Note: the Titan Juicer O.C.C. entry lists this armor at 180 M.D.C.; its own page prints 195, and the item page is taken as the authority for the item. Juicer Uprising p.68.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('mega-juicer-combat-armor', 'Mega-Juicer Combat Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 80.0, 55000, 'Black market 55,000 credits for the standard non-environmental version, 65,000 for the full environmental suit, which adds 10 lbs (4.5 kg)', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 130, 'Made by both Ultra-Tech Industries and Northern Gun, each of whom says the other stole the design. Very heavy: only supernatural strength, or a normal P.S. of 30 or higher, wears it without major penalties. Weight aside it is extremely flexible and gives excellent mobility to anyone who can carry it. Variable mobility: at a normal P.S. of 30+ or a supernatural P.S. of 20+, -10% prowl, -5% climb, swim, acrobatics and gymnastics, speed reduced 10%. Weaker wearers, down to P.S. 24 normal or 16 supernatural, are -25% prowl, -15% to the rest, speed reduced 30%. Below that the wearer CANNOT MOVE AT ALL. Juicer Uprising p.69.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('spiked-armor', 'Spiked Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 17.0, 30000, 'Black market 30,000 credits', 'Body slam or tackle 2D6 plus P.S. damage to unarmored humans; a Juicer with P.S. 25+ does 1 M.D. against M.D.C. armor or skin. Power slam, counting as two attacks, 5D6 plus P.S. bonus to S.D.C. targets and 1D6 M.D. to mega-damage structures and creatures. Supernatural strength adds 1D6 M.D. to hand to hand damage - treat a body slam as a punch and a power slam as a power punch.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 45, 'Very popular with Juicers who play combat sports like Juicer Football and Murderthon. The spikes are mega-damage material and will chip at M.D.C. alloys and injure supernatural creatures. Lightweight, mobile, and better protection than average - a favourite of Juicers, outlaws, and some adventurers and headhunters. Good mobility: -5% prowl. Juicer Uprising p.69.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('vibro-spike-armor', 'Vibro-Spike Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 18.0, 55000, 'Black market 55,000 credits; E-Clips not included', 'Body slam 2D6 M.D. against ALL targets; power slam, counting as two attacks, 4D6 M.D. Characters with supernatural strength add these to their basic hand to hand damage.', 1, NULL, 'E-Clip in a compartment on the lower torso; up to twelve hours of continuous use, and each activation drains a minute of charge even if used for less', NULL, 50, 'Spiked Armor with vibro-fields on the spikes. Many Juicers and other warriors love the idea; wiser people point out that a careless wearer can damage his own armor or injure himself by rubbing the live spikes against another part of his body - every hour they are left running there is a 01-22% chance he does exactly that. Good mobility: -8% prowl. Juicer Uprising p.69.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('man-killer-eba', 'Man-Killer EBA', 'rifts', 'armor', 40.0, 60000, 'Black market 60,000 credits', 'Body slam 2D6 plus P.S. S.D.C. against unarmored humans; a Juicer with P.S. 25+ does 1 M.D. against M.D.C. armor or skin. Power slam, counting as two attacks, 4D6 plus P.S. bonus to S.D.C. targets and 1D6 M.D. to mega-damage structures and creatures. Supernatural strength adds 1D6 M.D. to hand to hand damage.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 110, 'A heavy environmental suit for the most lethal combat conditions, trading speed and agility for superior mega-damage protection. Juicers who mean to fight power armor or supernatural opponents hand to hand wear this instead of the lightweight Juicer assassin armor. Its spikes hurt M.D.C. materials and supernatural beings and make grabbing him painful. Has all standard EBA features and can be used with a jet pack. Poor mobility: -20% prowl, -5% climb, swim, acrobatics and gymnastics, speed reduced 10%. A wearer with P.S. 23 or less also loses one attack per melee, is -1 on initiative, and has his speed reduced 30%. Juicer Uprising p.70.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71'),
('super-hide-armor', 'Super-Hide Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 20.0, 80000, 'Black market 80,000 credits, plus 1D6x10,000 credits for genuine dragon scale. Poor availability outside Kingsdale or the Federation of Magic, and uncommon even there.', 'Built-in claws are mega-damage weapons that parry mega-damage attacks without penalty and inflict 3D6 plus P.S. bonus S.D.C. A Juicer or other augmented human can make a power claw attack, counting as two attacks, for 1D6+1 M.D. Supernatural strength adds 1D6+1 M.D. to normal hand to hand damage when striking with the claws.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 70, 'Also called Dragon Scale or Dragon Skin armor: the hides of supernatural beings, treated and grafted onto a flexible articulated frame. Every suit is custom-made and often works in skulls, bones and other M.D.C. remains. M.D.C. VARIES with the materials - an average suit is 70-100, and true dragon armor runs 110-140; the stored figure is the bottom of the ordinary range. Weight is 20 lbs (9 kg) plus 10 lbs (4.5 kg) per 10 M.D.C. over 100. Mobility: a base -15% prowl with a further -1% per 5 M.D.C. over 100, plus -10% climb, swim, acrobatics and gymnastics, and speed reduced 10%. Armor with real dragon hide in it is very likely to enrage any dragon who sees it, and many will simply attack; some good characters find wearing the skins of sentient beings barbaric. Many Dragon Juicers buy it after their conversion and do not care who objects, which is why some places call it Dragon Juicer Armor. Note: the Dragon Juicer O.C.C. entry lists Dragon Skin Combat Armor at 100 M.D.C., within the range this page prints. Juicer Uprising p.71.', 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71')
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS juicer_uprising_gear_a FROM gear
 WHERE source_book = 'Rifts World Book 10: Juicer Uprising p.61-71';
SELECT slug, name, category, cost, mdc FROM gear
 WHERE slug IN ('drug-crash', 'titan-plate-armor', 'super-hide-armor', 'rocket-boots')
 ORDER BY slug;

-- Records this run. One row per run rather than per file: every statement above
-- guards itself, so this script is safe to re-run and safe to run early.
-- See db/migrations/024-data-script-runs.sql.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-juicer-uprising-gear-a.sql');
